<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices rose 0.1 pct in March.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices rose 0.1 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following provisional data:</p>
<p>				    March	Feb	March 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.1	  0.2	  0.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     1.1	  1.6	  2.3</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    115.0	114.9	  113.8</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    107.8  -0.4    0.4    0.2</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    109.0   0.6    0.4    0.0</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    126.0   0.1    0.6    1.6</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    114.9  -0.7    0.0    3.9</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    130.6   0.5    2.3    2.8</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    130.4   0.2    0.6    1.9</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    110.1   0.1   -0.1    0.6</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    113.9   0.1    0.4    0.9</p>
</text>
